<title>USA: ALZA buys Bayer product.</title>
<headline>ALZA buys Bayer product.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>ALZA Corp said Tuesday it had acquired the Mycelex Troche product from Bayer AG for a $50 million upfront payment plus possible royalties.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Bayer will manufacture Mycelex Troche for ALZA and ALZA will make payments based on net sales.</p>
<p>Mycelex Troche is a slow-dissolving lozenge for the treatment and prevention of oropharyngeal candidiasis, a painful infection also known as oral thrush. The infection is prevalent in AIDS patients and others with compromised immune systems, such as those receiving chemotherapy.</p>
